        "explanation": "Senator Dorgan explicitly claims credit for a federal action by noting that he authored the legislation that successfully designated Bismarck State College as a National Power Plant Operations Technology and Educational Center."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Do NOT classify a text as credit-claiming (0) if the senator is merely engaging in position-taking (expressing support, opposition, or a policy stance on a bill, issue, or nomination), advertising (promoting town halls, private non-governmental awards, or public appearances), or symbolic gestures (e.g., condolences, memorials, or holiday greetings). Additionally, exclude instances where the senator is introducing or co-sponsoring a bill that has not yet passed, or engaging in ongoing advocacy (such as writing pressure letters or calling for audits) without a finalized, successful outcome.",
    "negative_examples": [
